==Trivia==
*In the Turkish, Korean, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Lumberjack's name translates to "Woodcutter". In the Chinese and Finnish language settings of the game, the Lumberjack's name translates to "Crazy Woodcutter" and "Logman" respectively.
*The Lumberjack is 1 of 7 troops that has had its movement speed classification changed, the others being [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Elite Barbarians]], [[Suspicious Bush]], [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Cannon Cart]], and the [[Mighty Miner]].
**The Lumberjack is the first troop whose movement speed classification was changed since the [[Version History#Balance Changes (24/8/2016)|24/8/2016 balance changes]].
*The Lumberjack is 1 of 22 troops that has been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being [[Skeletons]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Bats]], Elite Barbarians, [[Firecracker]], [[Rascals|Rascal Girls]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Heal Spirit]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Guards]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Sparky]], [[Phoenix]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Bandit]], and the [[Monk]].
*When attacking, the Lumberjack will say "''Chop chop!''" or “''Timber!''”. He also laughs.
**Along with the [[Knight]], [[Barbarians]], and Electro Wizard, he is voice acted by [https://www.imdb.com/name/nm1423395/ John Mondelli].
**The Lumberjack is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Mega Minion]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Dark Prince]], [[Bowler]], Ram Rider, Electro Wizard, [[Princess]], [[Ice Wizard]], [[Magic Archer]], [[Mother Witch]], [[Fisherman]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Boss Bandit]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Little Prince]], and the [[Terry]].
* While not available as a troop in Clash of Clans, the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Super_Valkyrie Super Valkyrie] troop in the former is likely inspired from the Lumberjack, with both being fast melee troops that deal high damage per second, and drop a Rage spell after death. However, unlike the Super Valkyrie, the Lumberjack's [[Rage]] is identical to ones not used by the Lumberjack.
*The Lumberjack is responsible for creating [[The Log]], which is hinted at on several different occasions: 
**The Lumberjack's description states ''"and hunts The Log by night"''.
**In The Log's description, it states the cause of its creation was "''a spilt bottle of Rage''", which is a property exclusive to the Lumberjack.
**In the Clash of Clans [https://youtu.be/O__Lo2FQJKo?si=-HOvOgWxC1jNOeI- No More Clashmas?! commercial], The Log had a flashback to its creation where the Lumberjack is seen spilling the Rage spell in a forest.
**By an [[Emotes|Emote]] where the Lumberjack cowers because The Log towers over him.
**In the Clash-A-Rama episode "[https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/%22%27Twas_The_Night_Before_Clashmas%22 Twas The Night Before Clashmas]", the Kings search for a Clashmas Tree. They ignore the Lumberjack's majestic one, and decides on a smaller and ugly looking tree. The agitated Lumberjack tries to destroy it, but slips and drops his Rage spell, which converts the tree into The Log.
*The Lumberjack, Ram Rider, Phoenix, and the Fisherman are the only normal spawning {{Rarity|Legendary}} troops that do not fall from the sky when deployed.
*During the Lumberjack's deploy time, he can be seen drinking his bottle of Rage.
*The Lumberjack's rage drop animation used to be smooth, rather than the rigid one we have today. This animation was removed in an unknown update.
*The [[Card Mastery]] task "Rage of Empires" is a reference to the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Age_of_Empires Age of Empires] games series.
*The Lumberjack is the subject of a few Emotes.
**The Lumberjack All Seeing Emote is a reference to [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_Strange Dr. Strange].
**The Lumberjack Cheers Emote was originally going to appear in December of 2023, but did not make it to the game until the January of 2024.
**In the [https://youtu.be/fe6vI5RiqAQ?si=sCO1l_NmT850bvbQ Trophy Road intro video], there was an Emote that showed the Lumberjack spilling [[Elixir]] from his mouth. However, this Emote never made it to the game.
*The Lumberjack was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|decks]] of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Lumberjack was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/pRfrjMiHbQA?si=P2kVLJUlXH1SZoHm Clash Royale League 2021 Tournament], by a player called Mugi.
**The Lumberjack was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/vRrgTfqRdpw?si=YDASUydL7qNm9QZz Clash Royale League 2023 Tournament], by a player called Mugi.
*The Lumberjack has had balance changes that were planned for it but were not added to the game. More specifically:
**On 12/12/2022, the Rage was supposed to be added higher damage and a pushback of 0.3 tiles, but [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-42-balance-wip was pulled back last minute].
**The initial balance change for Lumberjack on the [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/1/2025)|8/1/2025 balance changes]] was a 5% damage increase and a Rage duration decrease to 5.5 seconds (from 6 seconds), but the damage increase was raised to 6% [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-67-balance-wip-january-2025 last minute].

